window.docContents[29].resolve({"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/The-generated-indexes/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--The-generated-indexes--Kinded-records-and-operations":{"contents":"Neither table needs an annotation to decide membership. A kinded record is a structure at least\none of whose fields is a registered carrier applied to a kind; a kinded operation is a definition\nwhose result type is one. @[kindCarrier] is the only opt-in, and it is already required for the\naudit.\n\nFor a record the useful column is the notation, because the fields are where @[pkc_math_symbol]\nattaches and a rendered equation's readability is decided.\n\n* Record* Field* Carrier* Kind* Notation* AvsConfig* two* Quantity* pureNumber* * Bounds* hi* Quantity* dl* * * lo* Quantity* dl* * DemoConfig* scale* Quantity* dl* * CholRowQ* l20* Quantity* reflectivity* * * l21* Quantity* reflectivity* * * l22* Quantity* reflectivity* * MiniMironovCoeffs* ndA0* Quantity* refractiveIndexKind* * * taub0* Quantity* relaxTimeKind* * * sigbF0* Quantity* conductivityKind* \n\nFor an operation it is the kind signature together with the authored crossings its body routes\nthrough — which makes the row a contract rather than a signature, since an operation that changes\nkind must reach a sanctioned crossing to do it.\n\nField projections are excluded. MironovNK.nd satisfies the criterion literally, its result type\nbeing Quantity nIndexKind α, but it is the record's accessor rather than an operation on kinds and\nis already a row of the table above.\n\n* Operation* Argument kinds* Result kind* Crossings* attenuationQ* paramB, vegetationIndex* attenuationK* * lavsForwardQ* paramA, paramB, paramC, backscatter, vegetationIndex, reflectivity* backscatter* * lavsResidualQ* paramA, paramB, paramC, backscatter, vegetationIndex, reflectivity, backscatter* backscatter* * d* * length* * dFake* * length* * v* * speed* * τ* * time* * avsForward* dl, dl, dl, dl, dl, dl* dl* * byPolarization* dl, dl* dl* * combined* dl, dl* dl* * decay* dl* dl* * gain* dl* dl* * grad* dl* dl* * letExample* dl* dl* * model* dl, dl* dl* * noted* dl, dl* dl* * ofN* * dl* * residual* dl, dl, dl* dl* * scaled* dl* dl* * scaledByTwo* dl* dl* * shared* dl, dl* dl* * twiceBound* dl, dl* dl* * lenA* * length* * lenB* * length* * lenF* * length* * massA* * mass* * a* * lengthKind* * aSpec* * lengthKind* * b* * lengthKind* * bSpec* * lengthKind* * doubled* * displacement* * east* * displacement* * up* * displacement* \n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009The generated indexes","header":"31.10.3. Kinded records and operations","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/The-generated-indexes/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--The-generated-indexes--Kinded-records-and-operations"}});